{"page": 12, "text": "Capital additions of $317.6 million, for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, were mainly for exploration wells including the Bubale-1X (Block CI-709) and Bubale West-1X (Block CI-103) wells in C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire; the Hai Su Vang-3X (Golden Sea Lion), Block 15-1/05 and Lac Da Trang (White Camel) North-1X, Block 15-1/05 wells in Vietnam; and the Banjo #1 (Mississippi Canyon 385) and Cello #1 (Mississippi Canyon 385) wells in the Gulf of America. In the third quarter of 2026, Murphy successfully appraised the Bubale discovery offshore C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire with the Bubale West-1X well, which encountered approximately 88 feet of net oil pay in the Turonian reservoir and 10 Table of Contents NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (CONTINUED) Note D \u2013 Property, Plant and Equipment (Continued) additional hydrocarbons in the deeper Albian reservoir. The Company also announced an oil discovery at the Lac Da Trang (White Camel) North-1X exploration well offshore Vietnam, encountering approximately 131 feet of net oil pay. Murphy also achieved first oil from the Lac Da Vang (Golden Camel) development offshore Vietnam. In the second quarter of 2026, Murphy announced a discovery at the Bubale-1X (Block CI-709) exploration well in C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire, with the well encountering 100 feet of net pay across two reservoirs. In addition, Murphy concluded the Hai Su Vang (Golden Sea Lion) appraisal program for Hai Su Vang-2X (Block 15-2/17), Hai Su Vang-3X (Block 15-1/05) and Hai Su Vang-4X (Block 15-2/17) appraisal wells in Vietnam. In the first quarter of 2026, Murphy announced the successful discoveries of the Banjo #1 and Cello #1 (Mississippi Canyon 385) exploration wells in the Gulf of America, which encountered 50 feet and 30 feet of net pay, respectively. In addition, the Company announced a successful appraisal well Hai Su Vang-2X (Golden Sea Lion), Block 15-2/17, in the Cuu Long Basin, located approximately 40 miles offshore of 