{"page": 32, "text": "27 Table of Contents NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (CONTINUED) Note Q \u2013 Leases Nature of Leases The Company has entered into various operating and finance leases such as a natural gas processing plant, floating production storage and off-take vessels, buildings, marine vessels, vehicles, drilling rigs, pipelines and other oil and natural gas field equipment. Options to extend lease terms are at the Company\u2019s discretion. Early lease terminations are a combination of Company discretion and mutual agreement between the Company and the lessor. Purchase options also exist for certain leases. During the third quarter of 2026, the Company commenced a finance lease for a floating storage and offloading vessel associated with its Vietnam operations. The lease term extends from September 2026 through October 2039, coinciding with the expiration of the relevant production sharing contract. The Company recognized a finance lease right-of-use asset of $103.4 million and a finance lease liability of $83.9 million in connection with this arrangement, with approximately $19.5 million in lease payments made prior to commencement. Finance lease right-of-use assets are contained in \u201cProperty, plant and equipment, at cost less accumulated depreciation, depletion and amortization\u201d on the Consolidated Balance Sheets. In October 2026, the Company entered into an agreement for the use of a deepwater drillship in the Gulf of America. The initial term of the agreement covers 10 wells. Based on current estimates of well durations and applicable rates, the aggregate consideration associated with the initial term is approximately $225 million to $325 million on a gross basis. Actual payments may differ based on the duration of each well and the contractual rate applicable during periods of operation, movement, standby, or other activities. The agreement also provides the Company with options for up to five additional wells at rates to be ag