{"page": 41, "text": "For the three months ended September 30, 2026 lease operating expenses decreased by $35.2 million and transportation, gathering and processing expenses decreased by $1.0 million compared to the same period in 2025. Lower lease operating expenses were primarily driven by lower Gulf of America workover costs, favorably impacted by insurance reimbursements at Marmalard and Neidermeyer and the non-recurrence of prior-year workover costs at Marmalard and Khaleesi. These decreases were partially offset by current-quarter workover costs at Mormont. For the nine months ended September 30, 2026 lease operating expenses decreased by $168.6 million, and transportation, gathering and processing expenses decreased by $11.7 million compared to the same period in 2025. Lower lease operating expenses were primarily driven by favorable Gulf of America workover costs, favorably impacted by insurance reimbursements at Marmalard and Neidermeyer and lower workover costs at Samurai and Khaleesi. In addition, lower FPSO rental fees at Cascade & Chinook also decreased lease operating expenses. The Company also received a one-time access fee related to the Lucius field, which further contributed to decreases during the period. These decreases were partially offset by higher Eagle Ford Shale operating costs related to workover costs and increased number of wells. Lower transportation, gathering and processing expenses were primarily due to lower sales volumes in the Gulf of America. 37 Table of Contents ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT\u2019S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS (CONTINUED) Results of Operations (Continued) Depreciation, Depletion and Amortization Expenses The Company\u2019s DD&A by geographic area were as follows:\nThree Months Ended\nSeptember 30, Nine Months Ended\nSeptember 30,\n(Millions of dollars) (Dollars per equivalent barrel) (Millions of dollars) (Dollars per equivalent barrel)\n2026 2025 2026 2025 2026 2025 2026 2025\nD